Batch E, run E1 (part 3). The sweeps of commit c6155b4's tests, float and bfloat16 timed in the same 20 rounds,
with the launches the kernels had before part 3 changed them: attention softmax 80 x 128 (forward and backward),
classifier forward 4096 x 1024, layer_norm 512 x 256 and 128 x 512, encoder 512 x 1024 for all three kernels.
adamw, gelu, residual and grad_norm already had the launches they keep. Google Colab, Tesla T4, -arch=native.
Only each test's sweep is kept (the Colab cell printed from the sweep's name to the end). layer_norm's sweep
failed its count: its bfloat16 weight_grad / bias_grad check compared two runs of rounded atomic adds within 2%,
which even the usual launch cannot pass (part 3, Section 12.3); its timings are valid and the check was replaced.

